            <ArticleTitle>Cutaneous anaplastic large cell lymphoma in a multiple sclerosis patient receiving Fingolimod.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-123</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S2211-0348(17)30329-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.msard.2017.11.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Previous reports of cutaneous neoplastic lesions secondary to Fingolimod treatment among multiple sclerosis patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Reporting a case of cutaneous large cell lymphoma in a multiple sclerosis patient during Fingolimod treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Case study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Our patient developed CD30+ cutaneous large cell lymphoma two years after initiation of Fingolimod treatment and her symptoms regressed following the cessation of treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This report indicates that cutaneous lymphoid neoplasms should be considered a possible side effect among patients receiving Fingolimod.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
